# EXPECT-VIOLATION: mirash:FaultCodeScopeShape
#
# SEED FIXTURE (ADR-0032 §8) — the template the fixture phase copies.
#
# An invalid fixture must fail for a SPECIFIC, DECLARED reason: the EXPECT-VIOLATION header above
# names the shape that must fire, and the validator fails the fixture if that shape stays silent
# (even if some OTHER shape happens to fire). That is what makes a red run meaningful — "the graph
# was rejected" is not evidence that the rule under test is the thing doing the rejecting.
#
# This is R4 — an unscoped fault code. 'F007' means one thing on a PowerFlex 40 and something else
# on a GS10; packs are family-keyed on disk, so scope is implicit and safe there, but the moment a
# code is lifted into the graph that scope is gone unless carried explicitly.

@prefix mira: <https://ontology.factorylm.com/mira#> .
@prefix ex:   <https://example.org/fx#> .

ex:manual a mira:SourceDocument .
ex:cite   a mira:Citation ; mira:cite_doc ex:manual ; mira:cite_locator "p.114" .

# No mira:scoped_to — the whole point of R4.
ex:f007_orphan a mira:FaultCode ;
    mira:fault_mnemonic "F007" ;
    mira:supported_by ex:cite .
